Z||000000||Dan||05-22-99||03:52 PM|||| I'm a new Fiero owner. I have an 85 4 cylinder. The car starves for fuel when the <br>tank gets down to a 1/4 tank. Is this normal? 
Z||000001||overlord||05-22-99||04:32 PM||||i have an 84 2.5<p>and have had the guage all the way to the end of the red..and hadnt ran out of fuel yet...sounds like some part of the fuel guage is inacurate somehow. either the guage itself or the float in the tank
Z||000002||Dan||05-22-99||04:55 PM|||| Tank gage is fine. Filled up tank from that point and it took 7.8 gal. It is consistant, every time it gets to that level, same problem. Maybe then, removal and inspection of tank is in order.
Z||000003||theogre||05-22-99||05:10 PM||||sounds like the pickup tube is short. Yup, you need to drop the tank to work on it. Nope, It ain't fun.
Z||000004||ChadMan||05-24-99||06:53 AM||||Dan, my advice is to just live with it until/unless your fuel pump needs replacing.  I have owned two 4-cyl Fieros (84 & 88) and both of them ran out of gas when the needle was just below an indicated 1/4 tank.  <p>Oddly enough, the 88 only holds 1/2 gal more fuel than the 84 (8.0 vs 8.5), though the Haynes and owners manuals both claim the 88 should hold almost 2 more gal.
Z||000005||Dan||05-25-99||11:31 AM|||| Yep, it does sound like a pickup tube problem. With the past problems with this model, I was wondering if any other folks <br>had this particular problem.This sure is a great forum.You Fiero enthaustist are a valuable asset to a new Fiero owner,especially a guy who likes to fix 'em.<br>If there was another class problem,I would<br>have liked to know BEFORE I DROP THE TANK.<br>Thanks all. 
Z||000006||Eric||05-27-99||01:31 PM||||My 88 ran out of gas today with 1/8 of a tank showing on the gauge and stranded me.  People tell me the 88s hold 12 gallons of gas, but I don't think my car will hold over 10.  However, when I fill it up, the gauge never shows more than 3/4 of a tank.  The gauges on this car suck.
